  message: "RE-CHECK 2026-11-02 on dev ae02786fca (WI-jomik acceptance sweep, after PR #2004: shared resolvers no longer guess among tied candidates; PR #2006: a Rust method call never binds a free function). VERDICT: STILL_REPRODUCES. Repro run: The item’s acceptance fixture /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/jomik_member_recheck_11022026/scratch_B/fogoj/src/main.rs: fn a(){ let child: Child = Command::new(\"x\").spawn().unwrap(); child.wait_with_output(); } and fn b(){ let child = Command::new(\"x\").spawn().unwrap(); child.wait_with_output(); } in one file; hypergumbo survey + io-boundaries. Control /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/jomik_member_recheck_11022026/scratch_B/fogoj_ctl: the same file without a().. Observed: Two-function file: calls rust:src/main.rs:9-12:b:function -> rust:std::process::Child:0-0:wait_with_output:external_symbol L11; io-boundaries: ’ipc_recv ... std::process::Child.wait_with_output (2) <- a (src/main.rs:4) <- b (src/main.rs:9)’. Control (b alone): b -> rust:external:0-0:wait_with_output:external_symbol L6, and io-boundaries lists only the subprocess Command.new, with no ipc_recv.. Note: So b’s Child typing and its ipc_recv source come only from a’s annotation, which is the file-scope leak. The SWEEP of other analyzers’ per-file var_types maps was not checked. Fixtures: /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/jomik_member_recheck_11022026/scratch_*/."  # 0acd
